The **Get Torbie** button now keeps cream text on a darker copper background in both themes.
Its text contrast stays at least **6.31:1**, including the hover and keyboard-focus transitions.

<ThemedShot
  light="https://media.aylith.com/torbie/media/website-contrast-20260925-light.png"
  dark="https://media.aylith.com/torbie/media/website-contrast-20260925-dark.png"
  alt="Torbie's website with a focused download button and the interactive Claude Code terminal preview"
  width={2720}
  height={1800}
/>

The live preview keeps its terminal sessions, plugins, split panes and full-screen views after
a dependency refresh. Language switching, theme changes, navigation recovery and guide motion
are covered by browser checks.

<details>
<summary>Dependency and desktop compatibility details</summary>

The desktop app, built-in plugins, web frontend and website dependencies were updated together.
TypeScript 7 runs standalone checks; Angular and its tooling still require the TypeScript 6
JavaScript compiler API. Electron 44 uses a clipboard bridge to preserve Torbie's synchronous
plugin methods. Future builds require macOS 13+ and support x64 and ARM64; existing v1.0.0
downloads remain available, including the unsigned Windows builds.

This update does not publish a new desktop installer. See the
[dependency migration notes](https://github.com/aylith-labs/torbie/blob/main/docs/dependency-upgrades.md)
for the compiler constraints and native build changes.

</details>
